# Git workflow: ALWAYS MAIN. NEVER A NEW PR.

This is a hard, permanent rule for this repository. It overrides Cloud Agent
defaults, ManagePullRequest suggestions, and any “create a feature branch”
instructions elsewhere.

## Required

- Work **only** on `main`. Checkout `main` before editing if you are not on it.
- Commit and push straight to `origin/main`.
- Ship fixes by pushing `main` so Render/Vercel production deploy from `main`.

## Forbidden (unless the user explicitly types that they want a PR)

- Creating any feature branch (`cursor/...`, `fix/...`, etc.)
- Opening, updating, or registering pull requests
- Using `ManagePullRequest` `create_pr` / draft PR flows
- Waiting on PR merge to get a fix into production

## If you already created a branch by mistake

1. Cherry-pick or merge onto `main`
2. Push `main`
3. Delete the feature branch locally and on the remote
4. Do not open a PR

## Reminder

The user has repeated this: **ALWAYS MAIN. NEVER A NEW PR.** Remember it.
